{"id":"mahabharata-1-027","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":27,"title":"सप्तविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 27 · Why Garuda was born to humble Indra","summary":{"en":"Shaunaka asks what Indra's fault had been. Indra once mocked the thumb-sized Valakhilyas, who in anger performed rites to create a second Indra; Kashyapa persuaded them to make the son born of their power king of the birds instead.","kn":"ಇಂದ್ರನ ತಪ್ಪೇನು ಎಂದು ಶೌನಕರು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಹೆಬ್ಬೆರಳಿನಷ್ಟು ಗಾತ್ರದ ವಾಲಖಿಲ್ಯರನ್ನು ಇಂದ್ರನು ಹಿಂದೆ ಅಪಹಾಸ್ಯ ಮಾಡಿದ್ದನು; ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ಅವರು ಇನ್ನೊಬ್ಬ ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗಾಗಿ ಯಜ್ಞಮಾಡಿದರು, ಕಶ್ಯಪನು ಅವರ ತಪಃಫಲದಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟುವ ಮಗನು ಪಕ್ಷಿಗಳ ಇಂದ್ರನಾಗಲೆಂದು ಒಪ್ಪಿಸಿದನು.","hi":"शौनक पूछते हैं कि इन्द्र का क्या अपराध था। इन्द्र ने एक बार अँगूठे जितने वालखिल्यों का उपहास किया था; क्रुद्ध होकर उन्होंने दूसरा इन्द्र उत्पन्न करने के लिए यज्ञ किया, और कश्यप ने उन्हें मनाया कि उनके तप से जन्मा पुत्र पक्षियों का इन्द्र बने।","te":"ఇంద్రుని తప్పేమిటని శౌనకుడు అడుగుతాడు. బొటనవేలంత పరిమాణంగల వాలఖిల్యులను ఇంద్రుడు ఒకప్పుడు ఎగతాళి చేశాడు; కోపించిన వారు మరో ఇంద్రుని కోసం యజ్ఞం చేశారు, వారి తపశ్శక్తితో పుట్టే కుమారుడు పక్షులకు ఇంద్రుడు కావాలని కశ్యపుడు వారిని ఒప్పించాడు.","ta":"இந்திரனின் குற்றம் என்ன என்று ஶௌனகர் கேட்கிறார். கட்டைவிரல் அளவுள்ள வாலகில்யர்களை இந்திரன் ஒருமுறை ஏளனம் செய்தான்; கோபமுற்ற அவர்கள் இன்னோர் இந்திரனைப் படைக்க யாகம் செய்தார்கள், அவர்களின் தவத்தால் பிறக்கும் மகன் பறவைகளின் இந்திரனாகட்டும் என்று கஶ்யபர் அவர்களை இணங்க வைத்தார்.","ml":"ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ തെറ്റ് എന്തായിരുന്നുവെന്ന് ശൗനകൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. പെരുവിരലിന്റെ വലുപ്പമുള്ള വാലഖില്യരെ ഇന്ദ്രൻ ഒരിക്കൽ പരിഹസിച്ചു; കോപിച്ച അവർ മറ്റൊരു ഇന്ദ്രനെ സൃഷ്ടിക്കാൻ യാഗം ചെയ്യുന്നു. അവരുടെ തപോബലത്തിൽ ജനിക്കുന്ന പുത്രനെ പക്ഷികളുടെ രാജാവാക്കട്ടെ എന്ന് കശ്യപൻ അവരെ അനുനയിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.27; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"शौनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कोऽपराधो महेन्द्रस्य कः प्रमादश्च सूतज ।\nतपसा वालखिल्यानां संभूतो गरुडः कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Suta, what was Indra's offense, and what his carelessness? How was Garuda born by the austerity of the Valakhilyas?"}},{"n":2,"text":"कश्यपस्य द्विजातेश्च कथं वै पक्षिराट्सुतः ।\nअधृष्यः सर्वभूतानामवध्यश्चाभवत्कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did the king of birds come to be the son of the brahmin Kashyapa, and how did he become unassailable and unkillable by all beings?"}},{"n":3,"text":"कथं च कामचारी स कामवीर्यश्च खेचरः ।\nएतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं पुराणे यदि पठ्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how did that sky-goer come to move and act as he pleased? I want to hear this, if the Purana tells it."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"विषयोऽयं पुराणस्य यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ।\nशृणु मे वदतः सर्वमेतत्संक्षेपतो द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"What you ask is a subject of the Purana. Listen, brahmin, as I tell it all briefly."}},{"n":5,"text":"यजतः पुत्रकामस्य कश्यपस्य प्रजापतेः ।\nसाहाय्यमृषयो देवा गन्धर्वाश्च ददुः किल ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the patriarch Kashyapa was performing a sacrifice, wishing for a son, the sages, gods and gandharvas gave him help, it is said."}},{"n":6,"text":"तत्रेध्मानयने शक्रो नियुक्तः कश्यपेन ह ।\nमुनयो वालखिल्याश्च ये चान्ये देवतागणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Kashyapa appointed Indra, and the sages, the Valakhilyas and other hosts of gods, to bring the firewood."}},{"n":7,"text":"शक्रस्तु वीर्यसदृशमिध्मभारं गिरिप्रभम् ।\nसमुद्यम्यानयामास नातिकृच्छ्रादिव प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra lifted a load of firewood the size of a mountain, matching his strength, and carried it easily, as if it were nothing."}},{"n":8,"text":"अथापश्यदृषीन्ह्रस्वानङ्गुष्ठोदरपर्वणः ।\nपलाशवृन्तिकामेकां सहितान्वहतः पथि ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the road he saw some tiny sages, each the size of a thumb joint, together carrying one stalk of a palasha leaf."}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रलीनान्स्वेष्विवाङ्गेषु निराहारांस्तपोधनान् ।\nक्लिश्यमानान्मन्दबलान्गोष्पदे संप्लुतोदके ॥","meaning":{"en":"They seemed withdrawn into their own limbs, fasting, wealthy in austerity, weak, struggling in the water of a cow's hoofprint."}},{"n":10,"text":"तांश्च सर्वान्स्मयाविष्टो वीर्योन्मत्तः पुरंदरः ।\nअवहस्यात्यगाच्छीघ्रं लङ्घयित्वावमन्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Intoxicated with his own strength and puffed up, Purandara laughed at them all, stepped over them, and went quickly on, insulting them."}},{"n":11,"text":"तेऽथ रोषसमाविष्टाः सुभृशं जातमन्यवः ।\nआरेभिरे महत्कर्म तदा शक्रभयंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages, filled with rage and deeply angry, then began a great rite that would terrify Indra."}},{"n":12,"text":"जुहुवुस्ते सुतपसो विधिवज्जातवेदसम् ।\nमन्त्रैरुच्चावचैर्विप्रा येन कामेन तच्छृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men of great austerity offered oblations into the fire according to rule with various mantras. Hear what they wished for."}},{"n":13,"text":"कामवीर्यः कामगमो देवराजभयप्रदः ।\nइन्द्रोऽन्यः सर्वदेवानां भवेदिति यतव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"May there be another Indra of all the gods, one who moves at will, has strength at will, and strikes fear into the king of the gods,\" those firm in vows thought."}},{"n":14,"text":"इन्द्राच्छतगुणः शौर्ये वीर्ये चैव मनोजवः ।\nतपसो नः फलेनाद्य दारुणः संभवत्विति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"May a terrible one be born today by the fruit of our austerity, a hundred times Indra in valor, strength and swiftness of mind.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"तद्बुद्ध्वा भृशसंतप्तो देवराजः शतक्रतुः ।\nजगाम शरणं तत्र कश्यपं संशितव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learning this, Indra, king of the gods, greatly distressed, went for refuge to Kashyapa of strict vows."}},{"n":16,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा देवराजस्य कश्यपोऽथ प्रजापतिः ।\nवालखिल्यानुपागम्य कर्मसिद्धिमपृच्छत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the king of the gods, the patriarch Kashyapa went to the Valakhilyas and asked whether their rite had succeeded."}},{"n":17,"text":"एवमस्त्विति तं चापि प्रत्यूचुः सत्यवादिनः ।\nतान्कश्यप उवाचेदं सान्त्वपूर्वं प्रजापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So be it,\" those truthful sages replied. Kashyapa the patriarch then said to them gently:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अयमिन्द्रस्त्रिभुवने नियोगाद्ब्रह्मणः कृतः ।\nइन्द्रार्थं च भवन्तोऽपि यत्नवन्तस्तपोधनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By Brahma's decree this Indra was made lord of the three worlds. And you too, ascetics, have worked for an Indra."}},{"n":19,"text":"न मिथ्या ब्रह्मणो वाक्यं कर्तुमर्हथ सत्तमाः ।\nभवतां च न मिथ्यायं संकल्पो मे चिकीर्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, you should not make Brahma's word false, and what I wish to accomplish should not be false to your intention either."}},{"n":20,"text":"भवत्वेष पतत्रीणामिन्द्रोऽतिबलसत्त्ववान् ।\nप्रसादः क्रियतां चैव देवराजस्य याचतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let there be an Indra of the birds, of great strength and spirit. And show favor to the king of gods who asks it.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"एवमुक्ताः कश्यपेन वालखिल्यास्तपोधनाः ।\nप्रत्यूचुरभिसंपूज्य मुनिश्रेष्ठं प्रजापतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus by Kashyapa, the ascetic Valakhilyas honored that best of sages, the patriarch, and replied:"}},{"n":22,"text":"इन्द्रार्थोऽयं समारम्भः सर्वेषां नः प्रजापते ।\nअपत्यार्थं समारम्भो भवतश्चायमीप्सितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Patriarch, this undertaking of ours was all for an Indra, and yours was for a son, as you desired."}},{"n":23,"text":"तदिदं सफलं कर्म त्वया वै प्रतिगृह्यताम् ।\nतथा चैव विधत्स्वात्र यथा श्रेयोऽनुपश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Accept this rite, which has borne fruit. Arrange it here as you see best.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु देवी दाक्षायणी शुभा ।\nविनता नाम कल्याणी पुत्रकामा यशस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just then the auspicious and renowned Vinata, daughter of Daksha, longing for a son, was in her vow."}},{"n":25,"text":"तपस्तप्त्वा व्रतपरा स्नाता पुंसवने शुचिः ।\nउपचक्राम भर्तारं तामुवाचाथ कश्यपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having practiced austerity, devoted to her vow, she bathed at the rite for obtaining a son and, pure, approached her husband. Kashyapa said to her:"}},{"n":26,"text":"आरम्भः सफलो देवि भवितायं तवेप्सितः ।\nजनयिष्यसि पुत्रौ द्वौ वीरौ त्रिभुवनेश्वरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Goddess, the undertaking you desire will bear fruit. You will bear two heroic sons, lords of the three worlds."}},{"n":27,"text":"तपसा वालखिल्यानां मम संकल्पजौ तथा ।\nभविष्यतो महाभागौ पुत्रौ ते लोकपूजितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the Valakhilyas' austerity and my intention, two highly fortunate sons will be born to you, honored by the world.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"उवाच चैनां भगवान्मारीचः पुनरेव ह ।\nधार्यतामप्रमादेन गर्भोऽयं सुमहोदयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed son of Marichi said to her again, \"Carry this embryo, of great destiny, without carelessness."}},{"n":29,"text":"एकः सर्वपतत्रीणामिन्द्रत्वं कारयिष्यति ।\nलोकसंभावितो वीरः कामवीर्यो विहंगमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of them, a hero honored by the world, a bird with strength at will, will make himself Indra of all birds.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"शतक्रतुमथोवाच प्रीयमाणः प्रजापतिः ।\nत्वत्सहायौ खगावेतौ भ्रातरौ ते भविष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The patriarch then said to Indra, pleased, \"These two bird brothers will be your helpers."}},{"n":31,"text":"नैताभ्यां भविता दोषः सकाशात्ते पुरंदर ।\nव्येतु ते शक्र संतापस्त्वमेवेन्द्रो भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"No harm will come to you from them, Purandara. Let your distress go, Indra; you will remain Indra."}},{"n":32,"text":"न चाप्येवं त्वया भूयः क्षेप्तव्या ब्रह्मवादिनः ।\nन चावमान्या दर्पात्ते वाग्विषा भृशकोपनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And do not again insult those who speak of Brahman, nor in pride slight the sages whose words are poison and who are quick to anger.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"एवमुक्तो जगामेन्द्रो निर्विशङ्कस्त्रिविष्टपम् ।\nविनता चापि सिद्धार्था बभूव मुदिता तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this, Indra went without fear to heaven, and Vinata, her wish fulfilled, was glad."}},{"n":34,"text":"जनयामास पुत्रौ द्वावरुणं गरुडं तथा ।\nअरुणस्तयोस्तु विकल आदित्यस्य पुरःसरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She gave birth to two sons, Aruna and Garuda. Aruna, of whom the lower body was missing, became the forerunner of the sun."}},{"n":35,"text":"पतत्रीणां तु गरुड इन्द्रत्वेनाभ्यषिच्यत ।\nतस्यैतत्कर्म सुमहच्छ्रूयतां भृगुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Garuda was consecrated as Indra of the birds. Descendant of Bhrigu, hear now his great deed."}}]}]}